@startuml DIAGRAM_05B_GRADING_REVIEW_EN
'==============================================================
' AIVES - AI SCORING & EXAMINER REVIEW (slide-ready, English, SIMPLE)
' Same Visual Paradigm look as DIAGRAM 5A:
'   - participant box: light blue fill, blue border, blue bold text
'   - life line: THIN DASHED vertical guide
'   - messages: numbered "1:", "2:", ... solid = call, dashed = return
'
' 8 lifelines kept, messages cut to a slide-friendly set.
'
' BUSINESS RULE (the point of this diagram):
'   The AI does NOT grade on its own. The submission is stored as
'   PENDING_REVIEW and stays ungraded until the EXAMINER authorizes
'   the AI grading for that result. Only then is the job queued.
'
'   1. Student finishes the viva -> submission stored (PENDING_REVIEW).
'   2. The EXAMINER opens the waiting submissions and authorizes AI grading.
'   3. Only now a job is queued -> Back-end Service (Grading) -> AI service
'      evaluates against the rubric and returns the score.
'   4. The examiner reviews the evidence, assigns the official score
'      (REVIEWED) and publishes (PUBLISHED).
'   5. The student reads the final result.
'
' Components (8 lifelines, left to right):
'   Finish handler . Hangfire . Back-end Service (Grading) . AI service
'   Result store . Examiner . DB . Student
'
' Verified against:
'   backend/Aives.Application/Viva/Services/VivaSessionService.cs   (FinishSessionAsync)
'   backend/Aives.Infrastructure/Queue/SessionGradingJob.cs         (queue "grading")
'   backend/Aives.Infrastructure/Queue/AnswerProcessingJob.cs        (answer job)
'   backend/Aives.Application/Viva/Services/SessionGradingService.cs
'   backend/Aives.Api/Controllers/ResultsController.cs              (review / publish)
'   ai-service/app/api/evaluation.py
'
'   After rendering, run:
'     python ops/_sharpen_svg.py DIAGRAM_05B_GRADING_REVIEW_EN.svg --dashed-lifelines
'==============================================================
title AI Scoring & Examiner Review (AIVES)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam defaultFontColor #000000
skinparam BoxPadding 8

'--- participant / actor / database boxes: light blue like VP ---
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #DAE8FC
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #4A7EBB
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderThickness 1.6
skinparam sequenceParticipantFontColor #1F3864
skinparam sequenceParticipantFontStyle bold
skinparam sequenceParticipantFontSize 15

skinparam sequenceActorBackgroundColor #DAE8FC
skinparam sequenceActorBorderColor #4A7EBB
skinparam sequenceActorBorderThickness 1.6
skinparam sequenceActorFontColor #1F3864
skinparam sequenceActorFontStyle bold
skinparam sequenceActorFontSize 15

skinparam sequenceDatabaseBackgroundColor #DAE8FC
skinparam sequenceDatabaseBorderColor #4A7EBB
skinparam sequenceDatabaseBorderThickness 1.6
skinparam sequenceDatabaseFontColor #1F3864
skinparam sequenceDatabaseFontStyle bold
skinparam sequenceDatabaseFontSize 14

'--- life lines: thin dashed guide ---
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #6C8EBF
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderThickness 1.4
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBackgroundColor #FFFFFF

'--- arrows: dark, call = solid, return = dashed ---
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #333333
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.6

'--- alt / group frame (light blue) ---
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #4A7EBB
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderThickness 1.4
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #F4F8FD
skinparam sequenceGroupFontColor #1F3864
skinparam sequenceGroupFontSize 13

skinparam titleFontSize 20
skinparam titleFontStyle bold
skinparam titleFontColor #1F3864

participant "Finish handler" as FH
participant "Hangfire\nqueue: grading" as HF
participant "Back-end Service\n(Grading)" as GR
participant "AI service" as AI
participant "Result store" as RS
actor "Examiner" as EX
database "DB" as DB
actor "Student" as ST

ST -> FH: 1: Finish the viva
FH -> RS: 2: Save submission
RS -> DB: 3: Persist (PENDING_REVIEW)

EX -> RS: 4: Open waiting submissions
RS --> EX: 5: List of ungraded results
EX -> RS: 6: Authorize AI grading
RS -> HF: 7: Enqueue grading job
HF -> GR: 8: Load grading context
GR -> AI: 9: Evaluate answers / rubric
AI --> GR: 10: Score + feedback
GR -> RS: 11: Store AI score
RS -> DB: 12: Persist (EVALUATED)

EX -> RS: 13: Open evidence / AI result
EX -> RS: 14: Save official score
RS -> DB: 15: Status = REVIEWED
EX -> RS: 16: Publish result
RS -> DB: 17: Status = PUBLISHED
ST -> RS: 18: View my result

note over GR,AI
  Internal Backend - AI protocol:
  - POST /ai/evaluate/session
  - Header X-Internal-Token
    (= AI_SERVICE_SECRET_KEY)
  - Base URL http://ai-service:8000
  - Timeout 300s
end note

note over HF,DB
  Hangfire queue:
  - Storage: schema `hangfire` in PostgreSQL
  - Server `aives-grading-*`: 1 worker,
    queue `grading` (server `aives-api-*`
    handles `default` / `answers`)
  - Retry: 30s -> 120s -> 300s,
    max 3 attempts (BR-17)
end note

note over EX,RS: The AI never grades on its own.\nGrading starts only after the examiner authorizes it.

@enduml
